      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 46: implementing the regime switch — pre-registration",
      "text": "The two parameter classes reverse the verdict: under frozen priors switching WORSENS the pooled median (5.08 → 5.62), under per-ride inverted physics it IMPROVES it (5.51 → 4.12). The bias column adjudicates — below 3%, ε_d is near-unbiased under frozen priors (+0.28) and badly biased under honest physics (−4.64), while ε_f = 0.20 is the mirror image (+5.90, +0.11). Below the threshold the coasting limit clamps, so the applied ε_d has median 0.544 against ε_f's 0.20, and that refund cancels the over-prediction of the frozen CdA = 0.40 (well above the 0.26–0.32 these riders invert to). So the rule is correct and the frozen grid's sub-threshold ε_d cells are accurate BY CANCELLATION rather than by fit.",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
